IMPORT prelude
IMPORT types

-- Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ)
-- Part 3 Subpart 5 -- Other matters (cll 61 to 64).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, 2026 No 339-1, retrieved 2026-09-11.
--
-- The four provisions that move the boundaries of the Act after enactment:
-- exemption orders (cl 61), regulations that add platforms, specified features
-- and excluded activities (cl 62), general regulations (cl 63), and the cl 64
-- review duty. Each is exercised by Order in Council on the Minister's
-- recommendation, and each recommendation carries a satisfaction test.

§ `Part 3 Subpart 5 -- Other matters`

§§ `61. Exemption order`

DECLARE `exemption recommendation` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 61(2)(a)
    `the Minister considered the digital content of the platform`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister considered the features of the platform`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister considered the users of the platform`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 61(2)(b) and (c)
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 61(3)
    `the Minister is satisfied the benefits outweigh the risk to children`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 61(2): the procedural preconditions are conjunctive.
GIVEN e IS A `exemption recommendation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 61(2) preconditions are met` IF
        e's `the Minister considered the digital content of the platform`
    AND e's `the Minister considered the features of the platform`
    AND e's `the Minister considered the users of the platform`
    AND e's `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`
    AND e's `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`

-- cl 61(1)(a): the exemption may relieve an operator from ANY OR ALL
-- requirements under the Act, including the cl 11 minimum age duty. The only
-- substantive limit is the cl 61(3) satisfaction test. See NOTES.md, OS-014.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 61
@export Decide whether the Minister may recommend an exemption order for an operator
GIVEN e IS A `exemption recommendation` @desc What the Minister considered, whether the regulator's advice was sought and considered, whether consultation occurred, and whether the Minister is satisfied that the benefits of the exemption outweigh the risk of children being exposed to harmful digital content and interactions.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may recommend an exemption order` IF
        `the section 61(2) preconditions are met` e
    AND e's `the Minister is satisfied the benefits outweigh the risk to children`

§§ `62. Regulations relating to age-restricted platforms`

DECLARE `regulation purpose` IS ONE OF
    `section 62(1)(a) -- specifying an internet service as an age-restricted platform`
    `section 62(1)(b) -- specifying a feature as a specified feature`
    `section 62(1)(c) -- specifying an activity for the definition of excluded service`

DECLARE `regulation recommendation` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `the purpose`                                                                       IS A `regulation purpose`
    -- cl 62(2) and (3): the consideration limbs for (1)(a) and (1)(b)
    `the Minister carried out the considerations required for this purpose`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 62(2)(b), 62(3)(b), 62(5)(a)
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 62(2)(c), 62(3)(c), 62(5)(b)
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 62(4): the test for (1)(a) and (1)(b)
    `the Minister is satisfied the regulations are necessary or desirable for the purpose of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 62(6): the test for (1)(c)
    `the Minister is satisfied the benefits of those services outweigh the risk to children` IS A BOOLEAN

-- cll 62(4) and 62(6) impose different satisfaction tests depending on which
-- limb of cl 62(1) the regulations are made under.
GIVEN r IS A `regulation recommendation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 62 satisfaction test is met` IF
    CONSIDER r's `the purpose`
    WHEN `section 62(1)(a) -- specifying an internet service as an age-restricted platform`
        THEN r's `the Minister is satisfied the regulations are necessary or desirable for the purpose of the Act`
    WHEN `section 62(1)(b) -- specifying a feature as a specified feature`
        THEN r's `the Minister is satisfied the regulations are necessary or desirable for the purpose of the Act`
    WHEN `section 62(1)(c) -- specifying an activity for the definition of excluded service`
        THEN r's `the Minister is satisfied the benefits of those services outweigh the risk to children`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 62
@export Decide whether the Minister may recommend regulations under clause 62
GIVEN r IS A `regulation recommendation` @desc Which limb of cl 62(1) the regulations are made under, whether the Minister carried out the considerations that limb requires, whether the regulator's advice was sought and considered, whether consultation occurred, and whether the satisfaction test for that limb is met.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may recommend regulations under section 62` IF
        r's `the Minister carried out the considerations required for this purpose`
    AND r's `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`
    AND r's `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`
    AND `the section 62 satisfaction test is met` r

§§ `63. Regulations relating to other matters`

DECLARE `general regulation recommendation` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 63(2) carries no satisfaction test, unlike cll 61(3), 62(4) and 62(6).
@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 63
@export Decide whether the Minister may recommend regulations under clause 63
GIVEN r IS A `general regulation recommendation` @desc Whether the regulator's advice was sought and considered, and whether the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may recommend regulations under section 63` IF
        r's `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`
    AND r's `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`

§§ `64. Review of this Act`

-- cl 64(1): the review must be COMMENCED, and a report prepared, within 2 years
-- after commencement. cl 64(2) requires presentation to the House as soon as
-- practicable after completion.

`months within which the review must be commenced` MEANS 24

§§ `Scenario fixtures`

`an exemption without the satisfaction test` MEANS `exemption recommendation` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "process followed, benefits not found to outweigh risk"
    `the Minister considered the digital content of the platform`                        IS TRUE
    `the Minister considered the features of the platform`                               IS TRUE
    `the Minister considered the users of the platform`                                  IS TRUE
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS TRUE
    `the Minister is satisfied the benefits outweigh the risk to children`               IS FALSE

`a sound exemption recommendation` MEANS `exemption recommendation` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "narrow exemption, benefits found to outweigh risk"
    `the Minister considered the digital content of the platform`                        IS TRUE
    `the Minister considered the features of the platform`                               IS TRUE
    `the Minister considered the users of the platform`                                  IS TRUE
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS TRUE
    `the Minister is satisfied the benefits outweigh the risk to children`               IS TRUE

-- A cl 62(1)(c) recommendation carrying only the cl 62(4) test, not the
-- cl 62(6) test that actually applies to that limb.
`an excluded activity on the wrong test` MEANS `regulation recommendation` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "new excluded activity, necessary-or-desirable only"
    `the purpose`                                                                       IS `section 62(1)(c) -- specifying an activity for the definition of excluded service`
    `the Minister carried out the considerations required for this purpose`              IS TRUE
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS TRUE
    `the Minister is satisfied the regulations are necessary or desirable for the purpose of the Act` IS TRUE
    `the Minister is satisfied the benefits of those services outweigh the risk to children` IS FALSE

`a new age-restricted platform by regulation` MEANS `regulation recommendation` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "service specified as an age-restricted platform"
    `the purpose`                                                                       IS `section 62(1)(a) -- specifying an internet service as an age-restricted platform`
    `the Minister carried out the considerations required for this purpose`              IS TRUE
    `the Minister sought and considered the advice of the regulator`                     IS TRUE
    `the Minister consulted any person the Minister thinks appropriate`                  IS TRUE
    `the Minister is satisfied the regulations are necessary or desirable for the purpose of the Act` IS TRUE
    `the Minister is satisfied the benefits of those services outweigh the risk to children` IS FALSE

§§ `Machine-evaluated cases`

-- cl 61(3): the satisfaction test is a precondition, not a consideration, so
-- perfect process does not carry a recommendation on its own.
#ASSERT `the section 61(2) preconditions are met` `an exemption without the satisfaction test` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister may recommend an exemption order` `an exemption without the satisfaction test` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Minister may recommend an exemption order` `a sound exemption recommendation` EQUALS TRUE

-- cll 62(4) and 62(6): each limb of cl 62(1) has its own test, and satisfying
-- the wrong one does not carry the recommendation.
#EVAL `the section 62 satisfaction test is met` `an excluded activity on the wrong test`
#ASSERT `the Minister may recommend regulations under section 62` `an excluded activity on the wrong test` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Minister may recommend regulations under section 62` `a new age-restricted platform by regulation` EQUALS TRUE
